[center][size=5][b][color=#ffd966]Crafting Queue[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3]See what you need, what you have, and which chest it's in.[/size][/center]

Ever walk up to the workbench and forget what the recipe needed, or which chest the planks were in? Crafting Queue keeps a small to-do list on screen: [b]Ctrl + right-click[/b] anything to add it, and the panel shows what you have, what's missing and where it is.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/add-and-panel.gif[/img][/center]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Add from almost anywhere[/b]
[list]
[*]Ctrl + right-click works on items, station recipes, buildings, town works, quest requirements, NPC requests, vendor orders and tech tree blueprints.
[*]Vendor orders ask only for what the order still needs: goods already delivered or waiting on the pallets count.
[*]If the panel is folded because a window is open, it unfolds for a moment so you can see the new task.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/add-anywhere.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Manage your queue[/b]
[list]
[*]Hover a task for its [b]− +[/b] and trash buttons and its pin. Hold [b]Shift[/b] to change the amount by 10.
[*][b]New: drag a task by its title to reorder it.[/b] A gold line shows where it will land, and the list scrolls on its own near the edges. Right-click or Esc cancels.
[*][b]Ctrl + mouse wheel[/b] over the panel changes the icon size, [b]Shift + wheel[/b] the text size.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/queue-controls.gif[/img][/center]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/reorder.gif[/img][/center]

[b]The recipe tree, only for what's missing[/b]
[list]
[*]A task asks to [i]have[/i] that many: what you already own counts, and the recipe below covers only what's still missing.
[*]If something can be made at more than one station, or with more than one recipe, flip between them with ◂ ▸. Each option shows its own station, yield and ingredients.
[*]Real yields: the ×N includes your perks and talents, including a zombie's if one works that station.
[*]Only what you can actually use: locked recipes and stations stay hidden, and show up on their own once you unlock them.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/recipe-switch.gif[/img][/center]

[b]See which chest has it[/b]
[list]
[*]Little parchment bubbles, in the game's own style, over the chests and storages in your zone show which of your materials each one holds.
[*]Hover a task in the panel to preview where its materials are, or pin it to keep them marked.
[*]Short here? Hover the row to see where else you have it: "Yard: 7".
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/chest-bubbles.gif[/img][/center]

[b]The button bar[/b]
[list]
[*]Seven buttons in the game's own item cells that slide out of the panel's [b]⋮ corner[/b]: down its side, or across its top. [b]Right-click[/b] the corner to switch between the two; click it again to tuck them away. Gold frame = on, shaded = off.
[*][b]Bag and chest:[/b] count what you carry, the chests of your zone, or both (the default, like the game when you craft).
[*][b]Total view:[/b] everything the queue needs in one list, one row per material, added up across all your tasks, with what's missing first.
[*][b]Eye[/b] (always visible), [b]pin[/b] (chest bubbles), [b]lock[/b] (move and resize) and the [b]trash can[/b] to clear the queue (click twice to confirm).
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/button-bar.gif[/img][/center]

[b]Peek at any recipe[/b]
[list]
[*]Hold [b]Alt[/b] over any item, in your inventory, a chest or the panel itself, to see its full recipe without adding it.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/alt-view.gif[/img][/center]

[b]And also[/b]
[list]
[*]Tasks that share a material split it in queue order: drag them to set priorities.
[*]Tasks leave the list on their own once you craft, pick up or buy what was missing.
[*]Stays out of the way: with a chest, station or the tech tree open, the panel moves aside or folds into a small tab. The eye keeps it always visible. It also hides whenever the game hides its own HUD (story scenes, placing a building) and while you prepare and fight a battle.
[*]Make it yours: open the lock, then drag the title to move the panel or its corner to resize it. Names and icons rearrange as you drag.
[*]Every button explains itself when you hover it.
[*]Options to hide the panel while the queue is empty, to put the buttons down the side or across the top, text size from 8 to 32, and the opacity of the whole panel or only its background.
[*]Settings in the game: with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] installed, everything is in ESC → Mods → Crafting Queue, with the panel shown next to the menu so you see every change right away.
[/list]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/main/docs/images/mods-menu.gif[/img][/center]
[list]
[*]Without the framework, [code]BepInEx\config\verto13.gk2.craftingqueue.cfg[/code] explains every setting in English and Spanish.
[*]One queue per save slot, saved safely. A new game never inherits the queue of a deleted save.
[*]The same size as the game's interface at any resolution (it uses the game's own UI scale), pixel-crisp. Very light (about 0.1 ms per frame). 16 languages, following the game's language.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Controls[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Ctrl + right-click[/b] – add to the queue
[*][b]Alt[/b] (hold) – show a recipe
[*][b]F3[/b] – show / hide the panel
[*][b]F4[/b] – detailed / compact recipes
[*]Hover a task – its − + and trash buttons, and its pin ([b]Shift[/b]: by 10)
[*]Drag a task by its title – reorder the queue
[*][b]Ctrl / Shift + wheel[/b] over the panel – icon / text size
[*]The button bar – what to count, the Total view, always visible, chest bubbles, the lock and the trash can
[*]Gamepad [i](experimental)[/i]: tap [b]R3[/b] on a slot to add it, hold R3 to see its recipe, R3 in the world to use the panel ([b]View[/b] switches to the Total view)
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[b]BepInEx 5 is required[/b] (skip step 2 if you already play with BepInEx mods).
[list=1]
[*]Close the game.
[*]Download [url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.5[/url]: the file [b]BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.5.zip[/b].
[*]In Steam, right-click [b]Graveyard Keeper 2[/b] → [b]Manage[/b] → [b]Browse local files[/b]. That's your game folder.
[*]Extract BepInEx into that folder, then this mod's zip (choose [b]Replace[/b] if asked). You should see a [b]BepInEx[/b] folder and [b]winhttp.dll[/b] next to [b]GraveyardKeeper2.exe[/b].
[*]Start the game and load your save: the [b]Queue[/b] panel appears at the top right.
[/list]
Your queue is kept when you update.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [code]BepInEx\plugins\CraftingQueue[/code] in your game folder.

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Graveyard Keeper 2 (tested on version 1.006).
[*][b]Required:[/b] [url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5]BepInEx 5.4.23.x[/url] (BepInEx_win_x64).
[*][b]Optional:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/42]GK2 Mod Framework[/url] 0.1.14 or later, for the in-game settings menu.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Good to know[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]No balance or gameplay changes, and your save is never touched: the queue lives in its own file per save slot.
[*]While you hold Ctrl, right-click adds to the queue instead of doing its normal action.
[*]"Have" counts what you carry plus the chests of the zone you're in, like the game does when you craft. Other zones only show up as a hint, and chest bubbles only cover the zone you're in.
[*]No network access, no data collection, no game files or assets included.
[*]Works alongside other mods.
[*]Still in beta, so expect a few bugs. Gamepad support is experimental.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#ffd966]Bugs and source code[/color][/b][/size]
Found a bug? Please report it in the [b]Bugs[/b] tab or on [url=https://github.com/VERTO13/GK2-CraftingQueue/issues/new/choose]GitHub[/url], with a screenshot and the file [code]BepInEx\LogOutput.log[/code] from your game folder.

